  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 2.0,
    "cls_id": "CB26111",
    "sub_id": "16406",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": "<div>評量方式 動作 1. 課堂學習：20%（學習討論、出席、課堂作業) 2. 期中考：20% 3. 個人作品 10% 4. 期末作品發表：50% (互評成績佔20%) 作品成績衡量標準：完整度、切題、創意與深度、表達能力</div>\n",
    "tpa_score_new_en": " ",
    "course_pol": "課堂規則\n(1)課堂出席率，占\"學習\"成績之10%，三堂以上曠課紀錄\"學習\"成績為0，平時課堂作業10%，遲交將扣分，未交成績為0。\n(2)考試出席，無故未出席考試，補考成績為該成績之60%計算，未考者0分計算。\n(3)學期專題作業，小組遲交將扣分，未繳交者0分計算。",
    "course_pol_en": "(1) Class attendance accounts for 10% of the \"learning\" grade. Three or more unexcused absences will result in a \"learning\" grade of 0. Regular class assignments are worth 10%; late submissions will receive point deductions, and non-submissions will receive a grade of 0.\n\n(2) For exam attendance, students who take a make-up exam without a valid excuse will result in 60% of the original score, and those who do not take the exam will receive a grade of 0.\n\n(3) For semester group projects, late submissions by groups will receive point deductions, and non-submissions will receive a grade of 0.",
    "course_rem": "出席率很重要，重視小組合作。",
    "course_rem_en": "Attendance is important, and we value group collaboration.",
    "ais_meno": "<div>(1)同學在學習、寫作、做報告的過程，在引用他人資料時，必須清楚記載作者出處來源，含線上、實體與影音資料，也要避免抄襲、作弊、捏造及不當協同合作等行為。(2)課程提供之文本、參考資料與ppt，在未獲作者同意下，也請勿私下流傳。</div>\n\n<div>(3)凡是學生曲解自己的學習任務、或損害學術任務之不端正行為，包括在作業或考試中作弊、剽竊、串改；或將他人完成的作品作為自己的作品；或未經教師批准和同意，提交相同或相似的論文、報告，以滿足多門課程的要求，成績以零分計算。</div>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>(1) When citing others&#39; materials in the process of learning, writing, and creating reports, students must clearly document the source attribution, including online, physical, and audiovisual materials. Students should also avoid plagiarism, cheating, fabrication, and inappropriate collaboration.</div>\n\n<div>(2) Course texts, reference materials, and PowerPoint presentations should not be shared privately without the author&#39;s consent.</div>\n\n<div>(3) Any student who misrepresents their learning assignments or compromises academic integrity, including cheating, plagiarism, or alteration in assignments or exams; submitting others&#39; work as their own; or submitting identical or similar papers or reports to fulfill requirements for multiple courses without instructor approval and consent, will receive a grade of zero.</div>\n\n<div><!-- notionvc: 19580b32-e305-46c5-af14-5e71633e86e9 --></div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
